    titre: 'We are getting married - Insurance needs',
    contenu:
      `
## We are getting married

Are you getting married, or have you already taken the big step at the altar? Congratulations! Now is the time to review your joint insurance situation.

## Living together

Household insurance for several people is cheaper than two separate policies. If you are insured with two different companies, you should cancel one of the contracts at the next possible renewal date. Also check whether the insured amount for your belongings still matches their actual value.

## Wedding gifts

Protect valuable items with valuables insurance. If one of these items is lost or stolen, the loss can be compensated. This also applies if you yourself lose or misplace an insured item, such as a valuable piece of jewellery.

## Honeymoon

With travel insurance, costs can be reimbursed if you are unable to take your trip or have to cut it short. You can take out travel insurance individually or for several people living in the same household.

## Retirement and estate planning

Marriage also settles matters of inheritance. Your spouse is, in principle, entitled to insurance benefits in the event of death. With life insurance, you can also protect each other in the event of death or disability. An investment fund can be worthwhile if you wish to save long-term for retirement or to fund an important project.

If one spouse mainly takes care of the children for an extended period and takes on the role of stay-at-home parent, it is important to seek advice on pension planning. This helps, in particular, to avoid gaps in AHV/AVS (old-age and survivors' insurance) contributions.
`,
